    "prose": {
      "guidance": "This corpus is numismatic scholarship: coin catalogues, hoard reports and dating\narguments. Each coin type is a thing in its own right — ruler, mint, denomination,\nmetal, weight, and when it was struck. Attributions are claims about a coin made by\na scholar, graded by the kind of evidence offered; later articles may dispute earlier\nattributions, and the dispute is worth surfacing.\n",
